# Ramification index over j=1728 equals ord_w(j-1728)

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.ramificationIndex_eq_ord_sub_of_restrict_eq_jLinePlace1728`
(`5f1a5448-3887-5ed9-a629-23d9fbc58e72`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `63381d0b-f86d-5012-83d1-8e9a2a773211`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Fix $N \ge 1$ and let $F_N = \mathbb{Q}(j_q, j_{q^N})$ be the modular function field, i.e. the
intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the
Laurent series $j_q = q^{-1}\cdot j\mathrm{NumQ}$ and by its image under the $q \mapsto q^N$
substitution homomorphism; regard $F_N$ as an algebra over the simple extension $\mathbb{Q}\langle
j_q\rangle$ via the inclusion of $\mathbb{Q}\langle j_q\rangle$ into $F_N$, and assume this
extension is integral. Let $w$ be a place of $F_N$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, that is, a valuation subring
of $F_N$ which contains the image of $\mathbb{Q}$, is not the whole of $F_N$, and is a principal
ideal ring. Suppose that the restriction of $w$ to $\mathbb{Q}\langle j_q\rangle$ — the valuation
subring obtained as the preimage of $w$ under the inclusion — equals
[`ModularCurve.jLinePlace1728`](def/ModularCurve_JLinePlaces.html#L50), the place of
$\mathbb{Q}\langle j_q\rangle$ transported along the isomorphism $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,\mathbb{Q} \cong
\mathbb{Q}\langle j_q\rangle$ (sending the variable to $j_q$) from the place of
$\mathrm{RatFunc}\,\mathbb{Q}$ attached to the irreducible polynomial $X - 1728$. Then the
ramification index of $w$ over $\mathbb{Q}\langle j_q\rangle$, defined as the least positive integer
of the form $\operatorname{ord}_w(\iota f)$ with $f \in \mathbb{Q}\langle j_q\rangle$ nonzero,
equals, as an integer, $\operatorname{ord}_w(j_q - 1728)$, where $j_q$ is viewed as an element of
$F_N$ and $\operatorname{ord}_w$ is minus the logarithm of the associated $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued
adic valuation.

This is the standard identification, for a place of the function field of $X_0(N)$ lying over the
point $j = 1728$ of the $j$-line, of the ramification index with the order of vanishing of $j -
1728$; it is the computational form in which ramification above the elliptic point of order $2$ is
handled. It is used in the counting of fibres over $j = 0$ and $j = 1728$, in the determination of
$\nu_2$ and $\nu_3$ for $X_0(N)$.

